> From: "Damien Dye" <damiendye@tiscali.co.uk>
> Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2003 17:32:15 -0000
>
> I have taken the Christmas period to update my LX machines firmware to SRM
> console instead of alpha bios, I have now got a few problems.
>
> 1) how do I make SRM autoboot from dqa0?

In SRM, do "show b*" (without the quotes) to see what the
boot-related variables are set to.  "bootdef_dev" controls
which device an argument-free "boot" command will use.
"boot_osflags" controls what flags are sent to aboot.  Most
should leave this one blank or put "0", if I understand
correctly.  If you have a custom aboot.conf file, set it to
the option number you want.

If you want the machine to boot automagically whenever it is
power cycled, reset, etc., then set "auto_action" to "boot"
(without the quotes).  However, if you do this, it might be
a bit difficult to get back to the SRM prompt.  IIRC, you
would need to stand on ^C while it powers up to interrupt it
from booting the OS.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net




