Hi,

> I have taken the Christmas period to update my LX machines firmware to 
> SRM
> console instead of alpha bios, I have now got a few problems.
>

> 1) how do I make SRM autoboot from dqa0?

Make sure you've set bootdef_dev and boot_osflags correctly. Then set 
auto_action
to "boot". It'll boot whatever you set the previous flags to.

> 2) Since the update my modem ( an internal ISA hardware modem) connect 
> to a
> peer without looping back on it self.?

I don't understand the problem you're describing. Is the modem plug and 
play or
does it use jumpers? What kernel are you running BTW and is it 
configured specifically
for 164LX and to use the SRM console as the bootloader?

You may also find the following useful. 
http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/srm.html

Peter
