> last message repeated 6 times
> pppd hangup (sighup)
> pppd modem hangup
> 
> 
> how do I stop the system echoing it's self?
> 

Does the modem work ok with minicom (or something like it)?

I've had this in my startup script for years.  I don't know if this will help
or not...

#
setserial /dev/ttyS2 irq 10 port 0x03e8 uart 16550A spd_vhi
setserial /dev/ttyS2
#
# shut the modem up
stty -echo < /dev/ttyS2

The first setserial line configures the modem IRQ, I/O port number,
UART type and sets it to high speed.  I used these values based
on what ISAPnP displays as configuration options.
The second line just prints the configuration so I can see that it's
set ok.  The last line I got from somewhere - I really don't recall
where - and it turns off the echoing of the input characters.

Alan




