Hello.

I've got a program called siocons
(http://www.identicalsoftware.com/yaroze/siocons.tgz)
that's used to transfer data via the serial port to a programmable playstation.
The program functions correctly under Linux/Intel, but hangs when I try to use it on my Alpha
box. I'm assuming this means that programming differences on the two
platforms are preventing it from working correctly. My programming skills
are limited, but I found a page stating that some programs assume a long
is 32 bits. With this in mind, I replaced all instances of long with
u_int32_t, but to no avail!

Can you offer any pointers which could help me get this program working?

Regards,

Richard.




