Richard Billingham <richard@billingham.co.uk> writes:

> My programming skills are limited, but I found a page stating that
> some programs assume a long is 32 bits. With this in mind, I
> replaced all instances of long with u_int32_t, but to no avail!

u_int32_t is probably an unsigned type (the C standard only specifies
uint32_t), while long is signed. Try using int32_t.

-- 
	Falk




