Nelson,
I'm thinking maybe what you read was meaning that none of the individual
raid devices should be nfs mounted over the network.  But you raid device
is perfectly fine nfs mounted.  Does that make sense?

Many large file servers with redundancy use raid in which all of the drives
are in one computer which creates a single raid device out of these
multiple drives.  This raid device is then nfs mounted over the network
with no problems.

You would not, however, want to us multiple nfs mounts from the network to
create a raid device.  This is where something like LVM would come into
play.
----
