On Tue, Jan 07, 2003 at 11:20:33AM +0100, Janez Gradisek wrote:
>
> I tried installing from CD but it didn't work. I used
> 
> >>>boot dqb1 -fi kernels/vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/hdb initrd=images/cdrom.img"
> 
> and got the following error messages:
> 
> ...
> aboot: booting from device 'IDE 0 11 1 1 1 0 0'
> 
> cb_open: failed IDE 0 11 1 1 1 0 0, dqb1.1.1.11.0
> aboot: unable to open boot device 'IDE ...0' c0...0
> aboot: kernel load failed (-1)
> halted CPU 0
> halt code=5

Interesting; it got "aboot" off the CD, but aboot couldn't get the
kernel, apparently.

What version of SRM are you running on your LX? Latest is V5.8, IIRC.

> With 2 floppies I use:
> 
> >>>boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1" 
> 
> and it goes well until either disk formating (just before installation of 
> packages) or network configuration (when clicking Next after entering the 
> IPs), when anaconda reports a bug.

What video card is installed?

Have you tried a "text mode" install?

> Hmm. I have CD-RW Waitec Storm 40/1 and it works fine under RH 6.2.

"Works fine" is different from "installs fine"; did you install 6.2
using the CD-RW?

> Another thing:
> At computer startup as the blue screen of the SRM appears I first get the 
> following message:
> ** mouse error **
> eb.ea.e9.e8.e7.
> 
> and then the SRM prompt >>>.
> Any ideas what this message means? Should I worry about it?

Well, you may need to worry; it indicates that the console isn't seeing
the mouse on the mouse's PS/2 port.

Does this affect mouse usage under X under 6.2? What kind of mouse is
it? Have you tried others?

