Is there a way to get a Radeon 7500 to work in a UP2000?
Earlier messages were that it should probably work, but
my first attempt was not successful.

With the Radeon 7500, on powerup all three keyboard LEDs
stay on and don't go off.  Hitting the reset button makes
the LEDs go off, but they don't do the usual blink on
then off thing that seems to accompany "testing the system".
I waited around to make sure it wasn't just the screen that
was blank.  Blindly, I typed "sound" on the keyboard, and
I did not hear the usual "Yellow Rose of Texas" from the
speaker.

SRM version is A5.8-81 08-MAY-2001 00:11:20.  With an
Oxygen VX1 card, before the SRM blue background comes up,
I see a version number of 2.16, but I'm guessing this is
the revision of the code in the VX1 rather than the code
in the BIOS emulator.

(The reason I wanted to try the Radeon 7500 PCI was it
is reported to work solidly with XFree86 4.1, while the
Oxygen VX1 has problems with XFree86 4.1.  When there is
action or cursor change, I see white sparkles on the screen.
More importantly, every once in a while the monitor reports
the sync rates are out of range, or the colors rotate.  I'm
preparing to move to RH7.2, and early testing shows the
screen goes bonkers about every 10 minutes with that combo.
When the screen does go bonkers, hitting ALT-CTRL-F8, waiting
a second or two, then hitting ALT-CTRL-F7 brings it back.)

Any suggestions?

Thanks.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net




