On Tue, Jan 07, 2003 at 02:59:16PM -0800, Robert M. Riches Jr. wrote:
> Is there a way to get a Radeon 7500 to work in a UP2000?

AFAIK you install at least 4.2.0 version of XFree86 and it works.  You
cannot expect anything reasonable with earlier versions.  You may need
"CrtScreen" option set to "1".  But my experience with these cards and
alpha are limited to AGP variants on UP1500s while you would need PCI.

> With the Radeon 7500, on powerup all three keyboard LEDs
> stay on and don't go off.

This may be a question of firmware which does not initialize your
card properly.  Can you find a newer SRM version for your board?

> (The reason I wanted to try the Radeon 7500 PCI was it
> is reported to work solidly with XFree86 4.1,

I do not know about that.  All my tests of Radeon 7500 with
XFree86 4.1 ended up in failures.

   Michal




