On Mon, 6 Jan 2003, Jay Estabrook wrote:

> When you say "hangs", do you mean the "siocons" program itself, the
> playstation, or both?

hello Jay.

the siocons program seems to hang during the transfer, the playstation
indicates that the transfer is 'done'. both the address and size reported
by the playstation are erroneous.

>
> >From a cursory look, the program appears to have two parts: the
> file-reading part (ecoff.c), and the downloading part (the rest).
>
> Do you know if the file-reading part works correctly? What I mean is,
> can you determine if the ecoff binary is read correctly by the code, and
> set-up correctly to be downloaded. If it IS, then you know that the
> problem is in the downloading...
>
>  --Jay++

while having a poke around with some rudimentary reporting, to try to
figure out if the size was being calculated wrongly i inserted a line in
handshake_send from file.c :

	/* write */
	if ((n = write(ps_fd, &dat, 1)) < 0)
	        perror("write");
	fprintf(stderr, "Writing: [%08x]", &dat); <-- inserted line
	return n;

this seemed to affect the size the playstation was reporting. the first
time i tried it the transfer worked and the game loaded correctly, however
on subsequent tries the transfer aborted with a 'sync error'. i'm guessing
i've stumbled on a time-critical portion of the code? redirecting the rest
of the output to /dev/null got the transfers working again.

i've tried the program with a few other transfers and they are hit and
miss - sometimes they work, sometimes they don't. curiouser and curiouser!

is there some difference in the timings between the intel/alpha platforms
that would affect the transfer?

Regards,

Richard.




