"Thursday AKA dr._john" <thursday@allidaho.com> writes:

> I got a line on a UP1500 mobo and processor at a decent price. The
> guy is in biz and will give me a 30-day warranty.  Should I buy it?
> Is there anything i should know, like it only works with one video
> card or will only run on Dead Cat Linux?

It's a nice machine IMHO :) For video cards, most should work; I have
an AGP Radeon 7500. You need at least XFree 4.2 for that.

UP1500 doesn't work with an unpatched Linux kernel, you can get a
patched kernel at ftp.harddata.com, or I can send you a patch.
ftp.harddata.com also has SRM updates.

> Seriously, what would be a good configuration for SRM, SCSI card, video
> & sound cards, NIC, and power supply?

NIC and sound are onboard and work OK. Power supply is recommended to
have 400W. The onboard IDE is not too bad, either, although I
experience long latencies with concurrent accesses (might be a general
Linux kernel problem, though).

-- 
	Falk




