On Wed, Jan 08, 2003 at 11:57:14AM +0100, Janez Gradisek wrote:
>
> I took a look at them and found this in console 4 and in tmp/syslog:
> 
> after  
>  	<6> Adding swap ...
> it started to complain about hdd, previously identified as ATAPI 48X CD-ROM
> driven by Uniform CD-ROM Driver Rev 3.12:
> 	<4> hdd: command error status 0x51 { DriveReady SeekComplete Error }
> 	<4> hdd: command error status 0x54
> 	<4> end_request: I/O errir, dev 16:40 (hdd), sector 1207772
> 	<4> hdd: irq timeout: status 0xd0 { Busy }
> 	<4> hdd: ATAPI reset complete
> 
> This probably suggests that CD-ROM is the problem. I'll try another CD-ROM. 

You didn't answer my earlier question: did you install 6.2 from CD
using the CD-RW? My guess is you installed 6.2 from floppy or from
an older CD-ROM, and the CD-RW is new, and never been installed-from.

Sometimes CD-RW do not behave like CD, and certainly the SRM console
will not have been tested against a CD-RW.

I would definitely try a "normal" CD-ROM instead.

Good luck, and let us know what happens.

