On Sat, Jan 11, 2003 at 05:51:46PM -0600, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> I'm updating my 7.2 installation with SRPMs from rawhide.

Most likely this will need some edits on spec files.  Configurations may
need some tweaks, for example.  Some prerequisites are often too strict
as well (a listed required version is often not the lowest possible but
the one which was on hands).  This has to be checked on case-by-case
basis.

> Is there a
> dependency list / tree for all the packages?

I am not aware of any readily available but you can produce something
like that yourself.  'rpm -qRp <some_package>' will list dependencies
for "<some_package>".  With a help of some scripts (perl?) and 'tsort'
you should get what you desire.

  Michal




