The harddisk of my UDB recently died. I tried to find another 2.5" SCSI HDD
but i guess they are pretty hard to come by :) Next idea i had was to find a
3.5" IDE HDD and use the onboard IDE connector. Unfortunately, so far i have
been unable to find a 2.5" extensioncord. I tried a (large) number of
computershops overhere (Netherlands) but they only seem to have 2,5" -&gt; 3.5"
conversionsets. Does anyone know a source where i could get them?
 
I also thought of getting a 3.5" HDD and mount in somehow in the unused
space above the PCI port. Some time ago i read somewhere that people
actually did this. The article/faq? warned about power usage of the HDD
since the powersupply is only 75 Watt. Does anyknow know if this is an issue
with the current HDDs (i can get a pretty cheap 40GB HDD)? Can i just put a
HDD in, or do they draw too much power from the PSU?
 
Any help would be appreciated.
 
Raymond
 
