The definition you give is for a WWN (fibre channel devices).  The WWID is
used to uniquely identify each disk as in following command:

	hwmgr -show scsi -id 51 -full


        SCSI                DEVICE    DEVICE  DRIVER NUM  DEVICE FIRST 
 HWID:  DEVICEID HOSTNAME   TYPE      SUBTYPE OWNER  PATH FILE   VALID PATH
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
   51:  0        omzspr01   disk      none    2      1    dsk0   [0/0/0]   

      WWID:0c000008:0020-37ff-fe4d-a00c


      BUS   TARGET  LUN   PATH STATE
      ------------------------------
      0     0       0     valid     


Bruce Hines
