Some time ago, on either this list or comp.os.linux.alpha,
it was mentioned that the open-source version of Tripwire
won't run on Alpha because it is not 64-bit clean.  I
attended a seminar given by Tripwire's CTO and asked him
(privately, not in the open Q&A) whether he knew whether
there were 64-bit-clean issues.  If there are general-
purpose 64-bit-ism problems, it would be a good thing for
Tripwire's business to clean them up in preparation for
Intel's Itanic and AMD's hammer/opteron/etc., even though
they would probably not consider Alpha to be commercially
worth their effort.

Anyway, can somebody point me to any documentation on
whether there are 64-bit-clean problems with Tripwire?
He said he'd route the question and get an answer to me.
If they ask me for more detail on what types of problems
are alleged, it would be helpful to have some pointers
for them.

Thanks.

Robert Riches
