The last version of tripwire that I know compiles on Tru64 unix is
	tripwire-1.3.
[I'm using it.]

I know that when 2.0 was first released, it did not compile on Tru64.
I don't recall if the commercial version or the Open Source version 
ever ran on Tru64.
If I remember correctly, Tripwire is not included in the OSS RPMs.

These are the instructions for Tru64.

1. cd include
2. mv over config.h_tru64
     config.h
3. cd ..
4. cp Makefile.tru64 to Makefile
5. make clean; make
6. [optional] make test
7. copy src/tripwire and src/siggen to
     /usr/local/etc/tripwire
     (install bsd is broken)?

T.T.F.N.
