I've been running RH 7.2 on my ps500a/u for about 8 weeks now.  The 
installation started out kind of crappy and then seemed to "learn" how to 
boot up and run on my box.  I'm using the stock download ISO with ext3 
filesystem.

Starting last week, and with almost regularity now,  the filesystem gets 
corrupted and has to be fsck-ed on reboot.  Sometimes the autofsck does the 
job but mostly I have to do it manually.  So far a single pass has goten me 
back in shape.  The msgs i get indicate a SCSI parity error, but when i boot 
Tru64 (on another disk) it runs up just fine.  

Is anyone else having this kind of problem?

jn

