There are two issues at compiling ogle with ccc: one is ccc differs from gcc on #defines with variable argument lists, and the other that I couldn't get ./configure to allow building shared libs with ccc.
re. frame rates: I tested a few more DVDs. 17 frames/sec seem to be a bit optimistic for the average DVD - it's more of the order of 10 fps on that pc164. But the same is true for mplayerxp and xine: their framerates are 4 to 6 fps.

Re. X: The latest X rpm from rawhide (4.2.99-4-20030121.0) compiles and works nicely (I only tried it on UP2000+ so far).

	Oliver



