Well, I got it compiled...and it works...sort of.

I had to apply a patch first to allow the module loader to 
recognize a couple of ELF relocatable symbol types; you'll 
probably need the same patch if you don't already have it.  I've 
posted the patch at 
http://skarpsey.dyndns.org/alpha-lfs/patches/XFree86-4.2-gprel.patch 
(you may also want to check out 
http://skarpsey.dyndns.org/alpha-lfs/alpha.html for other non-X 
fixes).  This fix got merged with XFree86-CVS, so it should be 
in the much-anticipated XFree86-4.3.0 release.

Now as for the "sort of" qualifier...I have an S3 Trio64.  It 
shows up with the following PCI listing in /proc/pci:

  Bus  0, device   9, function  0:
    VGA compatible controller: S3 Inc. 86c764/765 \ 
[Trio32/64/64V+] (rev 84).
      IRQ 19.
      Non-prefetchable 32 bit memory at 0xc000000 [0xfffffff].

I can get a half-working X server running on this card.  It pops 
up at 1024x768 with 16-bit color (yay!), however, it has some 
visual artifacts (shearing and snow, especially with a lot of 
window movement).  And if I try to Ctrl-Alt-F[1-6] back to a 
text terminal, it hangs the machine.

X clients seem to work just fine on this alpha box if I connect 
them to a remote X server over the network.  I've heard of 
people having only about a 30% success rate getting Trio64's to 
work on XFree86 4 and AlphaLinux (some specific PCI revs work, 
some don't), so I'm tempted to believe it's just a buggy driver.  
