> Can anybody tell me whether or not the UP2000+ onboard USB ports can be made to work? And if yes, how? The web is kind of fuzzy about this..

In case it's relevant, ...

I have a UP2000 rather than a UP2000+, and I have been told there
is basically no reasonable hope of using the on-board USB ports
on the UP2000-non-plus.  The folks at Harddata sold me a PCI card
with 5 USB ports, and it's working pretty well for two printers
and a scanner.  The ports are probably USB version 1.* rather than
version 2, so it doesn't have the blinding speed.  When I use
xsane with the scanner, it gets an I/O error the first time the
scanner warms up its light to do a preview, but I suspect that
is likely a scanner driver issue or an xsane issue.  Other than
that problem, it works great for printing and scanning.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net




